    "Explanation": [
      "The workflow shows all three build jobs succeeded (build-linux, build-mac, build-windows SUCCESS) while deploy FAILED. The deploy log lists the attached workspace contents as only ./meta/linux/build.txt, ./meta/mac/build.txt, ./meta/windows/build.txt — no app/ files — so `test -f app/linux/app.linux` failed with exit code 1. The root cause is that each build job's persist_to_workspace only lists `meta/\u003cplatform\u003e` in paths, never `app/\u003cplatform\u003e`, so the generated applications are never placed in the workspace. The requirement is that every platform's app reaches deploy via the workspace and deploy can verify and upload all three, so the correct fix is to persist the app paths (app/linux, app/windows, app/mac) in each build job. Storing artifacts on builds only would bypass the workspace requirement, fixing one platform leaves two tests failing, changing attach_workspace alone doesn't add missing files, and removing the verify step would hide the problem while uploading an empty artifact set."
    ],
    "ActualAnswer": [
      "{",
      "  \"builds_green\": true,",
      "  \"deploy_green\": false,",
      "  \"fix\": \"persist_app_paths\",",
      "  \"workspace_had_apps\": false",
      "}"
    ],
    "ExpectedAnswer": [
      [
        "{",
